WEBVTT

1
00:00.550 --> 00:10.691
This is Prometheus, the research assistant built on Crosswalk's behavioral data: the digital lives of ten million real people in the US, recorded day by day for five years.

2
00:10.691 --> 00:18.120
Ask it a question in plain English, and it answers from that record: what people really did, not what they said they would do.

3
00:18.120 --> 00:23.250
Here is what it does, how far it reaches, and why no other data source can do the same.

4
00:24.900 --> 00:27.035
Let's start with what it's built on.

5
00:27.035 --> 00:33.204
Crosswalk holds behavioral data on the digital lives of thirty million opted-in people around the world.

6
00:33.204 --> 00:39.076
Inside that is a ten million person US panel, census matched, so it looks exactly like the country.

7
00:39.076 --> 00:47.440
And it is longitudinal: the same people, recorded day by day, back to January twenty twenty-one, with yesterday's behavior on the file today.

8
00:49.090 --> 00:52.134
For each person, we see the entire digital life.

9
00:52.134 --> 00:53.720
Here is one ordinary day.

10
00:53.720 --> 00:56.003
The scores she checked at breakfast.

11
00:56.003 --> 00:57.335
The workout playlist.

12
00:57.335 --> 00:58.603
The posts she liked.

13
00:58.603 --> 01:01.013
The shopping cart she filled at lunch.

14
01:01.013 --> 01:03.550
The sneakers she looked at, three times.

15
01:03.550 --> 01:05.008
The dinner she ordered.

16
01:05.008 --> 01:07.545
The two episodes she watched that night.

17
01:07.545 --> 01:09.258
The thread she read in bed.

18
01:09.258 --> 01:10.653
The parlay she placed.

19
01:10.653 --> 01:12.619
In order, with the time of day.

20
01:12.619 --> 01:19.405
It comes from every screen she owns: the phone, the laptop, the connected TV, the tablet, the game console.

21
01:19.405 --> 01:22.830
And it all comes together under one ID, as one person.

22
01:22.830 --> 01:25.620
That record is what Prometheus answers from.

23
01:27.270 --> 01:32.651
When you ask Prometheus a question, it uses that longitudinal behavioral data to answer it.

24
01:32.651 --> 01:35.370
You ask the way you would ask it in a meeting.

25
01:35.370 --> 01:41.165
Prometheus finds the people who fit, reads five years of what they did, and calculates the answer.

26
01:41.165 --> 01:45.599
It comes back in percentages and in people, scaled up to the whole country.

27
01:45.599 --> 01:47.255
A quick count takes seconds.

28
01:47.255 --> 01:48.851
A full read, a few minutes.

29
01:48.851 --> 01:50.980
And it lands as a file you can send.

30
01:52.630 --> 01:53.780
Here is a real one.

31
01:53.780 --> 01:56.323
Who watches Landman, and what do they buy?

32
01:56.323 --> 02:02.558
Six point one eight million US viewers, half of them thirty-five to fifty-four, and just over half men.

33
02:02.558 --> 02:08.552
Their buying is everyday grocery and family goods first, at twenty-one percent of purchase signals.

34
02:08.552 --> 02:15.938
The lift against the average American sits in workwear, trucks and hardware: Carhartt, Wrangler, Tractor Supply, AutoZone.

35
02:15.938 --> 02:20.841
Eighty-one percent finish the season, and nearly half watch with a phone in hand.

36
02:20.841 --> 02:25.200
That is a marketing plan in one answer, and it took about three minutes.

37
02:26.850 --> 02:30.390
When you need the whole picture, the answer becomes a file.

38
02:30.390 --> 02:36.870
A full profile lands in your dashboard: the audience size and shape, with the US figure beside every number.

39
02:36.870 --> 02:42.210
The brands they buy and where they shop, ranked and indexed against the average American.

40
02:42.210 --> 02:45.750
What they watch, stream and listen to, and where they live.

41
02:45.750 --> 02:52.170
Thirty-five behavioral categories, hundreds of brands, one click to a CSV, and it will email itself to you.

42
02:53.820 --> 02:56.243
Profiles are one of nine kinds of answer.

43
02:56.243 --> 03:00.201
Which titles bring in subscribers, and which ones just get watched.

44
03:00.201 --> 03:03.688
The path people took from the first search to the purchase.

45
03:03.688 --> 03:06.583
Which touchpoint on a campaign really moved them.

46
03:06.583 --> 03:08.946
What a sponsorship is worth, in dollars.

47
03:08.946 --> 03:12.492
What a title does next, on the platform and at the checkout.

48
03:12.492 --> 03:22.064
What is trending across the internet, what people are most engaged with, and which IP they are buying: books, Wattpad stories, movie tickets and Broadway tickets.

49
03:22.064 --> 03:25.905
What is number one on FAST, podcasts, gaming, streaming and more.

50
03:25.905 --> 03:28.150
What the consumer is doing on a stock.

51
03:28.150 --> 03:34.177
And the digital twins: test a plan, a title or a price on ten million twins before you spend a dollar.

52
03:34.177 --> 03:36.659
And those are only the syndicated reports.

53
03:36.659 --> 03:42.686
Ask Prometheus literally any question you want to know about these ten million people, and it answers.

54
03:42.686 --> 03:44.340
The questions never run out.

55
03:45.990 --> 03:49.133
Why is this different from any other data source?

56
03:49.133 --> 03:51.250
Surveys tell you what people say.

57
03:51.250 --> 03:52.725
Ratings see one screen.

58
03:52.725 --> 03:54.457
Web analytics see one site.

59
03:54.457 --> 03:56.253
Card data sees one checkout.

60
03:56.253 --> 04:04.848
Prometheus sees one person across all of it, ten million times over, refreshed every morning, and census matched to the whole country.

61
04:04.848 --> 04:11.198
It is checked against real outcomes, elections, ratings, accounts opened, not against more surveys.

62
04:11.198 --> 04:14.020
And it answers in minutes, in plain English.

63
04:15.670 --> 04:23.555
Prometheus lives in the corner of every page in the dashboard, on your desktop, and in the API, so your own tools can ask it too.

64
04:23.555 --> 04:25.083
Type to it or talk to it.

65
04:25.083 --> 04:33.090
Ask it to email you the file, cut the audience to thirty-five to forty-four, build a new profile, or set up tracking on a campaign.

66
04:34.740 --> 04:36.105
Here is why you need it.

67
04:36.105 --> 04:39.459
The question that used to take six weeks now takes minutes.

68
04:39.459 --> 04:41.791
A quick lookup costs about fifteen cents.

69
04:41.791 --> 04:43.951
A full profile, three hundred dollars.

70
04:43.951 --> 04:52.480
And because every answer comes from the same ten million people, the same question gets the same answer every time, so you can act on it the same day.

71
04:54.130 --> 04:58.193
Ask Prometheus anything about ten million real people.

72
04:58.193 --> 05:00.300
Sign up at crosswalknyc.com.
